{"name":"Vanilla Cake","hex":"#fcf0ca","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vanilla","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tropical climbing orchid of the genus Vanilla (especially Vanilla planifolia), bearing podlike fruit yielding an extract used in flavoring food or in perfumes.","The fruit or bean of the vanilla plant."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of vanilla.","Standard, plain, default, unmodified, basic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanilla"},{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"White cake","blocks":[{"text":"White cake is a type of cake that is made without egg yolks. It was also once known as silver cake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Fair_Culinary_Competition_%282881682604%29.jpg/330px-Fair_Culinary_Competition_%282881682604%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_cake","wikidata":"Q104858815"},{"title":"Vanilla","blocks":[{"text":"Vanilla is a spice derived from orchids of the genus Vanilla, primarily obtained from the seed pods of the flat-leaved Mexican and Central American vanilla (V. planifolia)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg/330px-Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla","wikidata":"Q13241"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining fl